<title>USA: Chartwell adopts shareholder right plan.</title>
<headline>Chartwell adopts shareholder right plan.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chartwell Re Corp said Thursday its board adopted a shareholder rights plan.</p>
<p>The company said the plan calls for it to distribute a dividend of one preferred share purchase right for each outstanding share of its common stock.</p>
<p>It said the rights would be exercisable only if a person or group acquires 20 percent or more of its common stock or announces a tender offer that would lead to 20 percent ownership.</p>
<p>The record date for the rights distribution is May 22 and the rights will expire ten years later unless they are redeemed earlier by the company.</p>
<p>The rights distribution is not taxable to stockholders.</p>
<p>Chartwell Re's wholly-owned subsidiaries writes property, casualty, marine and aviation reinsurance.</p>
